@begin(section)

@title(Overview)

svers is a Common Lisp library for version comparison. It supports multiple
version comparison schemes.

This document is available as a
@link[uri="https://djha-skin.github.io/svers/manual.pdf"](PDF
document).

@begin(section)
@title(How It Works)

The key insight: by using the @link[uri="https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/ch-controlfields.html#s-f-Version"](Debian version comparison algorithm)
under the hood and simply normalizing version numbers from other schemes so
that they compare correctly, (almost) all of the version comparison algorithms
can be improved by optimizing just the Debian version comparison algorithm.

This architecture also makes it easy to add and maintain new version comparison
algorithms &mdash; just write a normalization function.

@b(Note on liberality:) svers is liberal in what it accepts. If you compare two
versions using @c(semver-vercmp) but one is not semver-compliant, svers will do
its best instead of failing. This is important because package version numbers
are set by maintainers, and it would be bad to break a build over a
technicality.

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Usage)

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(asdf:load-system "com.djhaskin.svers")
(use-package :com.djhaskin.svers)

;; Debian version comparison
(debian-vercmp "1.2.3~rc1" "1.2.3")  ;; => -1 (rc1 < release)

;; Maven
(maven-vercmp "1.0.0-alpha" "1.0.0-beta")  ;; => -1

;; RPM
(rpm-vercmp "1.0010" "1.9")  ;; => 1 (1.0010 > 1.9)

;; SemVer
(semver-vercmp "1.0.0-alpha" "1.0.0")  ;; => -1

;; RubyGem
(rubygem-vercmp "1.0.a10" "1.0.a9")  ;; => 1

;; Python (PEP 440)
(python-vercmp "1.0a1" "1.0b1")  ;; => -1 (alpha < beta)

;; Naive (punctuation-separated parts)
(naive-vercmp "1.2.0" "1.2")  ;; => 1
@end(code)

All comparison functions return:
@begin(list)
@(item) @b(Negative) if the first argument is older/less than the second
@(item) @b(Zero) if they are equal
@(item) @b(Positive) if the first argument is newer/greater than the second
@end(list)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Version Schemes)

@begin(section)
@title(Debian)

Full epoch and revision support per the
@link[uri="https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/ch-controlfields.html#s-f-Version"](Debian Policy Manual).

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(debian-vercmp "1:2.0-1" "1:1.9-2")  ;; => 1 (epoch 1 same, 2.0 > 1.9)
(debian-vercmp "1.2.3~rc1" "1.2.3")  ;; => -1 (rc1 < release)
(debian-vercmp "1.2.3-1" "1.2.3-2")  ;; => -1 (revision 1 < 2)
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Maven)

Supports qualifiers: @c(alpha), @c(beta), @c(milestone), @c(rc),
@c(snapshot), @c(ga), @c(final), @c(stable).

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(maven-vercmp "1.0.0-alpha" "1.0.0-beta")       ;; => -1
(maven-vercmp "1.0.0-rc1" "1.0.0")              ;; => -1
(maven-vercmp "1.0.0-snapshot" "1.0.0-alpha")   ;; => -1
(maven-vercmp "1.0.0" "1.0.0-ga")               ;; => 0 (ga = release)
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(RPM)

Fedora/RPM version comparison.

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(rpm-vercmp "1.0010" "1.9")    ;; => 1 (1.0010 > 1.9)
(rpm-vercmp "2.0.1" "2.0.1a")  ;; => 1 (numeric > alpha)
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(SemVer 2.0)

@link[uri="http://semver.org"](SemVer 2.0) support, including build metadata
ignoring and prerelease ordering.

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(semver-vercmp "1.0.0-alpha" "1.0.0")      ;; => -1
(semver-vercmp "1.0.0+build1" "1.0.0")     ;; => 0 (build metadata ignored)
(semver-vercmp "1.0.0-alpha" "1.0.0-beta")  ;; => -1
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(RubyGem)

Ruby gem version comparison.

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(rubygem-vercmp "1.0.a10" "1.0.a9")  ;; => 1
(rubygem-vercmp "1.0.0" "1.0.0.a")   ;; => -1 (prerelease)
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Python / PEP 440)

Full @link[uri="https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0440/"](PEP 440) support,
including local versions.

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(python-vercmp "1.0a1" "1.0b1")          ;; => -1 (alpha < beta)
(python-vercmp "1.0" "1.0+local")        ;; => -1 (local version newer)
(python-vercmp "1.0+local1" "1.0+local2") ;; => -1
(python-vercmp "1.0.dev1" "1.0a1")       ;; => -1 (dev < alpha)
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Naive)

Punctuation-separated parts comparison. This is the old rpmvercmp algorithm,
used for Python local version parts.

@begin[lang=lisp](code)
(naive-vercmp "1.2.0" "1.2")    ;; => 1
(naive-vercmp "1.2.a" "1.2.b")  ;; => -1
@end(code)

@end(section)

@end(section)

@end(section)

